Understanding Vendor Management Systems (VMS)
A Vendor Management System represents an enterprise-grade technological platform engineered to automate and streamline the complete lifecycle of external workforce engagement. These solutions provide centralized control over temporary staffing, contractor management, and services procurement through integrated modules covering requisitioning, supplier selection, onboarding workflows, compliance tracking, time/expense management, invoicing automation, and performance analytics.

By interfacing with HRIS, ERP, and financial systems, VMS platforms deliver unprecedented visibility into contingent labor expenditures while mitigating regulatory risks associated with worker misclassification and compliance violations—critical capabilities given that contingent labor now comprises over 40% of the typical enterprise workforce.

